A||||12||mr2meanie||Leaking water pump gasket ||||1||
Z||000000||mr2meanie||06-15-2001||11:04 PM||||I am working on an 88 Formula with a 2.8 V6. It appears to be leaking water out of the water pump base gasket. The water pump was freshly replaced and about 2 days later it started leaking so the car sat for 2yrs. I replaced the gasket today and it still leaks! I mean leaks bad!it appears to be leaking out of the bolts( and thsat would be past the gasket) I installed A gasket from Carquest and applied a thin (not thick) layer of Permatex water pump housing sealer to the gasket.Let it cure for 2.5-3 hours than filled it.... well it leaks just as bad. Where do you guys buy gaskets? at the dealer? any others have this problem? any advice you could give me would be great!  <P><BR>Thanks,<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||06-15-2001||11:07 PM||||did you put pipe dope, thread sealer on bolts?||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||06-15-2001||11:13 PM||||There is at-least one bolt that runs through a water-passage. Also, make sure the pump housing is good. It is possible the housing is cracked due to over-torquing the bolts. Plus, it is possible the timing covers leaking. A reman pump is only $12 also.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mr2meanie||06-15-2001||11:58 PM||||Thread sealer on the bolts huh?<BR>because thats where it leaks is out of the bolts but I figured it was cause of the gasket. Does everyone use that stuff? because the manual I have doesnt call for that. should I just use teflon tape? or is there another product?<P>MAN YOU GUYS ARE GREAT!<P>[This message has been edited by mr2meanie (edited 06-15-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by mr2meanie (edited 06-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||PBJ||06-16-2001||12:05 AM||||tape would work but there is squeeze tubes. This is not thread lock, is thread sealer.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||06-16-2001||12:08 AM||||I just teflon tape the threads of the bolts. I think the bolt that runss through the water passege is the bolt farthest forward on the pump housing, but my memory is a little hazy.||||reg||1
Z||000006||mr2meanie||06-16-2001||12:15 AM||||ok but too use the squeexe tube I need to drain the system and let all dry. and to do thatI need to take the pump off again. But If I useteflon tape I can put it on the bolts now right?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||fiero56||06-16-2001||12:26 AM||||If you pull the bolt(s)out one by one, you shouldn't need to drain the system, it will leak some, but not much more than it sounds like its doing now. I'd try teflon tape, it has worked for me everytime.||||reg||1
Z||000008||mr2meanie||06-16-2001||12:29 AM||||Thanks guys I never would have thought!<P>MR2's don't have stuff like that!<P>Thanks<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000009||mr2meanie||06-20-2001||11:03 AM||||OK guys trouble again. This thing still leaks now it appears as though it leaks out of the weep hole as well(?). I am gonna pull it apart now for the 3rd time and try it again with a new pump,gasket, and thread sealer on the bolts .||||reg||1
Z||000010||SteveJ||06-20-2001||11:12 AM||||Leaking out the weep hole is a classic pump failure. That pump was bad when you bought it.||||reg||1
Z||000011||sqoach||06-20-2001||11:50 AM||||If it's been leaking every time you've re-gasketed (is that a word?) it and stuff, then the pump must be bad. Especially if water is coming from the weep hole. Time for new pump.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||11
